  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Core Features**\n\nOkay, I\'m now drilling down into the specific features requested. I\'m focusing on the Pipefy inspiration and making sure I capture all the essentials for sales and internal workflows. I am trying to determine the scope of features.\n\n\n**Defining Core CRM Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the workflow management, making it closely resemble Pipefy, so it needs to include Kanban boards, list views, and a phases pipeline that is extremely customizable. I\'m focusing on the phases pipeline, its custom fields, and the conditional rules that\'ll be super useful. I am trying to determine all of the necessary sales workflows. I\'m also ensuring that these features scale to be applicable to internal workflows.\n\\n\\n\nOkay, I\'m now getting into customer communications. I\'m trying to add a native WhatsApp integration. I also want the system to store all message histories, provide template quick replies, and simulate direct link senders.\n\n\n**Adding Communication Functionality**\n\nI\'m now thinking about email integration, including compose, threading within cards, templates, and tracking delivery status. I\'m imagining real-time dashboards with KPIs and consultant productivity reports, complete with goal tracking. Then, I\'m moving on to automation triggers, actions, and a visual rule builder. I need to make the automations configurable. Finally, I\'m designing role-based access control with different user levels and a simulator.\n\n\n**Implementing Role-Based Access**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on user roles; Ants will only access their cards and team cards, Managers get everything plus reports and alerts, and Admins can configure automations, fields, and view audit logs. Next, I\'m moving on to implementing a notification system for managers, which will include a notification center with SLA warnings, high-value deal movement alerts, and consultant idle alerts.\n\nI\'m now thinking about export capabilities, for pipeline data, consultant reports, and audit logs to Excel/CSV or PDF. I will add a comprehensive audit log to track user actions, including card modifications, emails, and automation executions. Finally, I\'m checking existing packages, and considering `canvas-confetti`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 977972334
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
