  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining CRM Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the CRM application, and the TypeScript types are coming along nicely. I\'ve started by defining types for key CRM elements, specifically phases, using IDs and descriptive labels. I\'m aiming for a modular structure. I\'m focusing on \"Mapeados\" and \"Prospec\303\247\303\243o\" as initial phase examples.\n\n\n**Expanding CRM Phases**\n\nNow I\'m diving deeper into the CRM\'s phase structure. I\'m fleshing out each phase (\"Diagn\303\263stica,\" \"Proposta,\" etc.) to include custom fields. These fields will be specific to each phase, such as deadlines, channels, and budgets. I\'m also planning to incorporate customizable aspects like colors, service level agreement limits, and required data.\n\n\n**Defining CRM Infrastructure**\n\nI\'m now outlining key infrastructure elements. I\'ve begun defining the data structures for automations, notifications, and audit logs within the CRM. This includes trigger conditions and parameters for automations (e.g., exceeding value, card creation), notification types (e.g., SLA breach, deal won), and audit log details (user actions, timestamps). I\'ve also drafted templates for email and WhatsApp communications.\n\n\n**Constructing CRM Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing user roles and realistic lead assignments. I\'ve defined a team with diverse roles and skill levels. I am aiming to simulate 18+ realistic leads distributed across CRM phases, starting from \"Mapeados\" through to \"Perdido\". I am planning on incorporating real-world communication threads, Pipefy-like automations, and live goals, all with detailed audit logs.\n\n\n**Designing TopNav & Main Views**\n\nI\'m currently working on the application\'s top navigation and main views. I\'m focused on the workspace switcher, global search, and quick create features. I\'m planning to incorporate a real-time notifications bell with filtering options and an interactive dropdown. Additionally, I\'m designing a user role switcher to test permissions seamlessly. Finally, I\'m planning to include an export center for various data formats.\n\n\n**Developing Core Dashboards**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core dashboards and detailed metrics. I am including real-time sales KPIs such as conversion rates by phase, average ticket value, and sales cycle lengths. I\'m also planning to build individual consultant performance metrics, including rankings and closing rates. Individual goal tracking with progress bars will be a priority.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Controls**\n\nI\'m now focused on the administrative panel and user permissions. I\'m building granular controls for consultant roles (Admin, Manager, Consultant, Viewer), defining what they can export, edit, and view. I\'m also implementing individual monthly goal configuration. Furthermore, I\'m working on complete audit logs, recording all system actions for compliance. Lastly, I\'m designing a Pipefy-like modal for detailed card information with phase-specific fields and selectors.\n\n\n**Defining Phase-Specific Data**\n\nI\'m now detailing the specific data points needed for each CRM phase. For example, in \"Mapeado,\" I\'m including fields for mapping date, prospecting channel, lead profile (ICP), profile link, and initial score. Each phase will have its own tailored data points. This is evolving quite rapidly.\n\n\n**Integrating Communication Channels**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial communication channels into the CRM. I\'m focusing on \"Ganho\" phase data like closed value and billing methods. I\'m building a WhatsApp integration with chat timelines, quick templates, and even attachment simulations. I am planning on integrating an email composer with threads, templates, and open tracking. Also, I\'m working on an activities and tasks checklist.\n\nI\'m also working on detailed card histories and an audit trail, as well as an AI assistant.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 493461054
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
