  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Persistence Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the architecture for storing and retrieving a large volume of leads in Supabase. I\'m focusing on structuring a \"leads\" table with relevant data (customer information and assigned consultant) and designing pagination and search functionalities for efficient data retrieval.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Schema Design**\n\nI\'ve specified the schemas for the `leads` table, including crucial fields like `id`, `title`, `company_name`, contact details, assignment info, the 12 phases, and interaction data. I\'m focusing on key details like `tags`, `checklist`, `custom_fields`, timestamps, and the structure of `lead_interactions`.\n\n\n**Defining Interaction Logging**\n\nI\'m now detailing the schema for `lead_interactions`, focusing on crucial fields to store comprehensive interaction data. I\'ve defined fields for interaction `type`, `channel`, `sender`, and content. I\'m carefully considering how to represent metadata using JSONB for flexibility and am including timestamps. Indexing is designed for efficient retrieval based on lead and date.\n\n\n\n**Outlining Supabase Functions**\n\nI\'m currently mapping out Supabase function logic, including `fetchLeads` with extensive filtering, and how `fetchLeadInteractions` queries are structured. I\'m building functions to `createLead`, `updateLead`, `moveLeadPhase`, `addLeadInteraction`, and `deleteLead`. I\'m focused on the correct parameters for each function and how to manage credentials in a secure manner.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 844703112
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
