  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Supabase Integration**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started fleshing out the Supabase integration architecture. Currently, I\'m focusing on the `CRMContext`. It checks for the presence of credentials, and I\'m planning out how it will handle both configured and unconfigured states. I am considering the implications of authentication too.\n\n\n**Implementing Supabase Actions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the CRUD operations with Supabase. Creating, updating, deleting, and moving leads are all being mapped to corresponding functions (`createLeadInSupabase`, `updateLeadInSupabase`, etc.) which also update local state when successful. I am also working through fetching a lead\'s interactions on-demand and adding new interactions. I\'m focusing on the offline behavior now.\n\n\n**Developing Supabase Integration UI**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface elements for Supabase integration. A new modal, `SupabaseSetupModal.tsx`, will handle URL and key input, and provides a pre-made SQL script for setup, allowing one-click database creation and migration. I\'m also planning connection testing and status indicators. A Supabase status pill in the header will show connection status, while `CardModal.tsx` will fetch and display a lead\'s interactions on-demand, including various types of related data.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 29
      nanos: 355624376
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
