  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Field Identifiers**\n\nI\'ve homed in on field identification. It seems there\'s a potential inconsistency between using `field.key` versus `field.id`, specifically in line 486. In the `PhaseFieldDefinition`, `id` is a string and used as the field key. I\'m focusing on ensuring uniformity in how we reference these identifiers throughout the codebase, making sure both `field.id` and `field.key` are utilized consistently. I\'ll need to go over required fields and transitions to ensure everything checks out, as well.\n\n\n**Defining Transition Rules**\n\nI\'m now mapping out the transition rules between different stages. I\'ve got the rules for \"Mapeado\" to \"Prospec\303\247\303\243o\", and \"Prospec\303\247\303\243o\" to its possible destinations defined. The fields required during transitions to \"Diagn\303\263stica\" or follow-up states are clear, including the specific fields for each destination. The subsequent stages, \"Diagn\303\263stica\" and \"Proposta\", are also being evaluated.\n\n\n**Mapping Transition Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now detailing the required fields and permitted destinations for various transition scenarios. Specifically, I\'ve outlined the necessary inputs for moving to \"negociacao,\" including \"servicosAdquiridos,\" \"validadeProposta,\" and \"valorInicialProposta.\" I\'ve also clarified the conditions for follow-up stages, including required fields like \"dataProximoFollowup.\" Furthermore, I\'ve established the fields for \"perdido\" and \"ganho\" destinations, such as \"motivoPerda,\" \"valorFechadoFinal,\" and \"dataFechamento.\" This will be used to generate a dedicated rules engine.\n\n\n"
