    thinking: "**Clarifying the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the underlying cause: in Tailwind CSS v4, the `dark:` classes won\'t apply to specific elements without the custom variant `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));`. The system media query `prefers-color-scheme: dark` is the sole determinant of dark mode activation when this variant isn\'t defined. This behavior ignores classes like `.dark`, `.dark *` otherwise.\n\n\n"
